<%# The shared look for form controls, described in docs/UI_STYLE_GUIDE.md:
    `field` for every box a person types into or picks from (text, email,
    number, date and time inputs, text areas, drop-downs), and `button` with
    a `button-primary`, `button-secondary` or `button-danger` variant.

    Bare CSS rules, no <style> tag, so a layout can put them inside the style
    block it already has. The voice layout writes its CSS by hand and its specs
    read that one block.

    A .css template, rendered with `formats: :css`, not an .html one: in
    development Rails wraps every HTML partial in <!-- BEGIN … --> comments,
    which CSS does not read as comments. The file name ended up in the first
    selector and the whole .field rule was silently dropped.

    Why it exists: fields had drifted into a dozen variants of a 1px
    light-grey border with no padding, and caregivers typed into the wrong box
    or read a drop-down as plain text. A field has to be findable at a glance,
    for people who are not looking closely.

    Buttons are filled, never white with an outline, because a white box with
    a border is what a field looks like. "Replace this link" and "Stop this
    link" were read as form fields until they were given a fill.

    The rules set only how a control looks, never where it sits. Width and
    margin stay as utilities on the element, and a utility written beside
    `field` (say text-sm on a compact drop-down) still overrides it, because
    the Tailwind CDN injects its styles after this block. %>
.field {
  border: 2px solid #9ca3af;
  border-radius: 0.375rem;
  background-color: #fff;
  color: #111827;
  font-size: 1rem;
  line-height: 1.5rem;
  padding: 0.5rem 0.75rem;
  box-shadow: 0 1px 2px 0 rgb(0 0 0 / 0.05);
}
/* Chrome ignores line-height on a select; without a height it sits 4px
   shorter than the text box beside it. */
select.field { padding-right: 2rem; height: 2.75rem; }
.field::placeholder { color: #6b7280; opacity: 1; }
.field:focus {
  border-color: #2563eb;
  outline: none;
  box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px rgb(59 130 246 / 0.35);
}
.field[readonly], .field:disabled { background-color: #f3f4f6; }

.button {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  gap: 0.5rem;
  /* The height of a field, so a button beside one lines up with it (the
     task list's Filter sat 4px short of the drop-downs). It is also the
     smallest comfortable tap target. */
  min-height: 2.75rem;
  padding: 0.5rem 1rem;
  border: 1px solid transparent;
  border-radius: 0.375rem;
  font-size: 0.875rem;
  font-weight: 600;
  line-height: 1.25rem;
  cursor: pointer;
  box-shadow: 0 1px 2px 0 rgb(0 0 0 / 0.15);
}
.button:focus-visible { outline: 3px solid rgb(59 130 246 / 0.5); outline-offset: 2px; }
.button-primary { background-color: #2563eb; color: #fff; }
.button-primary:hover { background-color: #1d4ed8; }
.button-secondary { background-color: #e5e7eb; color: #1f2937; border-color: #d1d5db; }
.button-secondary:hover { background-color: #d1d5db; }
.button-danger { background-color: #fee2e2; color: #b91c1c; border-color: #fca5a5; }
.button-danger:hover { background-color: #fecaca; }
.button:disabled { opacity: 0.5; cursor: not-allowed; box-shadow: none; }
